{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 formalisation of the Erdős–Rado negative stepping-up lemma in its order-type form, for arities three and above and for at least two colours.\nFix an ordinal kappa; a colour count mu ≥ 2; and a target order type theta = omega^alpha with alpha > 0, so that theta is additively indecomposable. The theorem proved is, for every natural number r: if some colouring of the (r+3)-subsets of kappa by ordinals below mu admits no monochromatic subset of kappa of order type theta, then some colouring of the (r+4)-subsets of 2^kappa admits none either, using the same number of colours.\nThe construction compares two unrelated orders on 2^kappa -- an arbitrary well-order, and the lexicographic order given by the first place two sets differ -- and reads a colouring off the pattern of agreement between them along a chain, together with the sequence of discrepancies. Two colours are spent marking the chains where those patterns first deviate, and on the well-behaved chains the colouring copies the given one along the discrepancy map.",
